  "warnings": [
    "Baseline scenario: no transfer of any kind. All impact medians equal their baselines by construction and annual cost is zero.",
    "Support estimates poststratify national survey crosstabs onto population cells; no fitted hierarchical model.",
    "No cost-of-living adjustment across metros; federal poverty thresholds applied uniformly.",
    "Unsourced parameters (marked TODO in model/params.py): labor_supply_elasticity upper bound (0.25): the literature reports participation elasticities, not earnings lost per dollar transferred, so no published estimate exists in this functional form, effective_tax_rate (non-refundable cap): a statutory MARGINAL rate used to approximate TOTAL liability; JCT measured average effective rates are far lower, so this under-binds the cap.",
    "Poverty thresholds for 1- and 2-person households use the 'householder under 65' variant; the sample does not carry householder age. Does not affect child poverty.",
    "Metro results come from a 2,000-household oversample per metro. Intervals are roughly 3.9x wider than the national ones.",
    "Non-refundable credits are capped using a flat effective tax rate, not a tax calculator.",
    "Poststratification method: mrp.",
    "ev_dfp_parents: no sample_size published, so no observation variance can be computed. Dropped (NOT imputed).",
    "ev_dfp_nonparents: no sample_size published, so no observation variance can be computed. Dropped (NOT imputed).",
    "MRP fitted on 16 crosstab observations across 2 dimension(s): census_region, income_band. Partial pooling, so no MIN_EVIDENCE_N exclusion is applied -- 2 thin record(s) are USED at reduced weight: ev_yg2107_inc_100p, ev_yg2107_reg_ne.",
    "Estimated survey house effects (logit scale, median): morning_consult +0.049; yougov_economist -0.049. Spread 0.098 logits ~ 2.5 points at the midpoint -- instrument effect, removed from the population estimate.",
